Task aggregate-406
SQLite schema:
CREATE TABLE accounts_406(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, active INTEGER); CREATE TABLE charges_406(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER, amount INTEGER, settled INTEGER); CREATE TABLE refunds_406(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER, amount INTEGER, approved INTEGER);
Obligations: Return one row for EVERY active account: id, net. Net is total settled charges minus total approved refunds, treating missing totals as zero. Include negative and zero net accounts. Multiple charges and refunds can belong to the same account. Order by id.
Public example data: {"accounts_406": [[772, 1], [10, 1], [670, 1], [534, 1], [542, 1], [321, 1], [417, 1], [781, 0], [62, 1]], "charges_406": [[1, 10, 34, 1], [2, 10, 17, 0], [3, 10, 31, 1], [4, 670, 2, 1], [5, 670, 37, 0], [6, 670, 1, 1], [7, 670, 1, 1], [8, 534, 31, 1], [9, 542, 4, 1], [10, 321, 30, 1], [11, 417, 35, 1], [12, 417, 14, 0], [13, 417, 34, 1], [14, 417, 5, 1], [15, 781, 14, 1], [16, 781, 18, 0], [17, 781, 12, 1], [18, 781, 3, 1], [19, 62, 34, 1], [20, 62, 37, 0]], "refunds_406": [[1, 772, 26, 1], [2, 670, 32, 1], [3, 670, 26, 0], [4, 534, 20, 1], [5, 534, 5, 0], [6, 542, 15, 1], [7, 321, 17, 1], [8, 321, 9, 0], [9, 321, 25, 1], [10, 321, 33, 1], [11, 417, 27, 1], [12, 781, 26, 1], [13, 62, 16, 1], [14, 62, 23, 0], [15, 62, 3, 1], [16, 62, 33, 1]]}
Write a reusable SQL query valid for all databases satisfying this schema and obligations, not just these example rows.
Optional procedural memory:
SELECT a.id, (SELECT COALESCE(SUM(c.amount),0) FROM charges c WHERE c.account_id=a.id AND c.settled=1) - (SELECT COALESCE(SUM(r.amount),0) FROM refunds r WHERE r.account_id=a.id AND r.approved=1) AS net FROM accounts a WHERE a.active=1 ORDER BY a.id;
